MAP DATA
  Coastline: Natural Earth 1:50m admin-0 countries (public domain, default view), via world-atlas 2.0.2
  (Mike Bostock, ISC licence), read from the npm CDN by extract_aus.mjs and
  decoded with topojson-client 3.1.0 (Mike Bostock, ISC licence) -> demo/vendor/topojson-client.min.cjs.
  Only the two Australian rings (mainland, Tasmania) are kept, in demo/aus.js; no borders are drawn.
  Licence texts in demo/vendor/.
  Rainfall bands: ~90 approximate long-term annual rainfall values typed in by hand (main.js STN) and
  inverse-distance interpolated; schematic only (stated on the end card). The 50 Ma -> today map is an
  illustrative uniform "drying" of today's pattern, not a palaeoclimate reconstruction.

